# Agent Quality Loop

Use `.cursor/skills/agent-quality-loop/SKILL.md` as the single public workflow entry.

Route three axes independently:

- intent: align / diagnose / implement / accept / release / resume;
- assurance: fast / standard / formal;
- authority: read / local-write / exact current-turn external action.

Select `ask-plan-code-qa` only as the bounded code implementation adapter and `review-gate` only as the read-only independent review adapter. Reuse the parent contract and emit one user-facing summary.

- Package entry: adjacent `manifest.json` is version/distribution truth; routine ALIGN may start from `references/contract-presets.md`; optional mechanical hooks live in `integrations/cursor-hooks/` (never semantic acceptance).
- The parent AQL leads with exactly one adaptive user result summary; adapters return receipts only. Follow the information priority and Result Detail Budget in `contracts.md`; do not append a parallel machine status strip or force routine success through a long template.
- After ACCEPT/FAIL stop: lightweight RETRO may write project `lessons.md` (disclose diff); ALIGN injects active lessons; ACCEPT checks recidivism.
- ALIGN applies `collaboration-profile.md` defaults when present (phrase lexicon; the explicit current-turn instruction wins); RETRO may sediment 0–2 observed profile candidates per `references/personalization.md`; learned preferences never raise authority.
- ALIGN grounds the compile per the grounding ladder in `references/contracts.md`: verify load-bearing referents read-only before the freeze; prefer authoritative sources over model memory for external facts; disclose premises contradicted by observation before any edit (never fabricate the referent); a requested mechanism compiles as outcome + hypothesis; depth per the ladder tiers.
- Native-medium artifacts (incl. code via behavior replay): final-consumer framing + cold consumer probe required for `user_observable_result` PASS; blind consumer only when (`formal` or experiential) and host has subagents; else acceptor cold-consumes before implementer narrative / honest `NOT_RUN`.
- Multi-agent: divergence probe / blind consumer per host support; subagent output = evidence, not acceptance. `formal`/high-ambiguity creative: explicit ALIGN OK; disclose contradictions.
- Repair delta: a fix/lesson/replan is done only when the next taker sees a different actionable state — not “noted.”
- Resume: prefer inspectable reality over envelope/transcript memory; persist only negotiated agreements on the minimal carrier already in use.
- Path change: in-scope route switches need three-line disclosure (assumption / observation / kept·changed·stopped); goal or authority changes return to ALIGN.
- Formal/high-ambiguity ALIGN needs observable `success_observables` + decidable `counterexamples`; decision-changing counterexamples must be run before `user_observable_result` PASS; same-shape thrash ≥2 emits an unlock pack; inject lessons only when `Applies when` matches.

Never let an adapter claim `ACCEPTED`, enter release, or raise authority. Never let `full` publish/deploy. Inspect every dry-run side-effect path before execution.
